      "message": "Shenghan Gao\n\n\"Hey, this commit actually breaks the NFC driver and causes NFC to be not recognized by the system (not appear in the system settings menu at all). Upon a deeper investigation, I found out why this issue occurred:\n\nLineageOS’s Soong config (vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigSoong.mk#L76) always fallbacks to TARGET_INIT_VENDOR_LIB if the flag is set. Since sm8250-common still sets this variable android_device_xiaomi_sm8250/BoardConfigCommon.mk#L81, and cmi build script no longer does after the migration (commit 820e726 | AOSP), BoardConfigSoong ends up re-initializing the wrong vendor init using the common device\u0027s init file at the end, overriding cmi\u0027s device vendor init via soong done in device.mk. This breaks NFC on the device.\n\nAs a temporary workaround, resetting the flag to empty by adding the line TARGET_INIT_VENDOR_LIB :\u003d(empty) in cmi’s BoardConfig.mk overrides the flag from the common device config, fixing the issue (tested and confirmed). Although ideally, this should be addressed by migrating the Makefile vendor init in sm8250-common.\"",
